(version 1)

# SOLAR-GLOW DRH v4.0 — TRIPLE-FAB ENVELOPE (PCBWay ∩ OSH Park ∩ JLCPCB)
#
# Retargeted 2026-07-27 (PCBWay ∩ OSH Park), extended 2026-08-08 to include JLCPCB. These floors
# are the per-parameter INTERSECTION of three fabs, so one board file can be ordered from any of
# them without re-checking anything. The point is interchangeability: PCBWay for fast, cheap
# prototypes and the hard-gold production run; OSH Park After Dark (black FR4 + clear mask) for
# the naked "midnight" variant; JLCPCB as the ENIG-only volume alternate — and, uniquely among
# the ENIG-only pair, the one that stocks the production 0.6 mm thickness.
#
#   parameter           PCBWay      OSH Park     JLCPCB      governs       gate here
#   ------------------  ----------  -----------  ----------  ------------  ---------
#   trace width         0.100 mm    0.1524 mm    0.100 mm    OSH Park      0.152 mm
#   clearance           0.100 mm    0.1524 mm    0.100 mm    OSH Park      0.152 mm
#   drill (plated)      0.200 mm    0.254 mm     0.150 mm    OSH Park      0.254 mm
#   via annular ring    0.150 mm    0.127 mm     0.050 mm    >> PCBWay <<  0.1499 mm
#   copper -> edge      (n/s)       0.381 mm     0.200 mm    OSH Park      0.381 mm
#   PTH pad annular     0.150 mm    0.127 mm     0.180 mm    >> JLCPCB <<  0.1799 mm  (conditioned)
#   PTH hole -> copper  (n/s)       (n/s)        0.280 mm    >> JLCPCB <<  0.2799 mm  (conditioned)
#   pad hole -> hole    (n/s)       (n/s)        0.450 mm    >> JLCPCB <<  0.4499 mm  (conditioned)
#   NPTH drill          (n/s)       (n/s)        0.500 mm    >> JLCPCB <<  0.4999 mm  (conditioned)
#
# Two inversions now, not one. OSH Park is LOOSER on annular ring (5 mil vs PCBWay's 6 mil), so
# PCBWay governs vias; and JLCPCB is LOOSER than everyone on trace/space/drill but TIGHTER on
# every hole-adjacency number — its 1 oz PTH pads need 0.18 mm of ring where a via needs only
# 0.05, its plated holes want 0.28 mm to foreign copper, any hole pair involving a pad wants
# 0.45 mm wall-to-wall, and it will not drill an NPTH under 0.50 mm at all. Those four are
# genuinely new axes: neither earlier fab published a limit the board could get near, so nothing
# gated them. Each JLC rule below is CONDITIONED so it binds only the object class JLC constrains
# — the via fleet keeps its PCBWay-governed 0.1499 ring and is untouched by the 0.1799 pad rule.
#
# Where the board actually sits on the four new axes (measured 2026-08-08, pcbnew sweep): the
# only PTH pads are the eight M2 mounts at 0.700 mm annular (3.9x the JLC floor); worst plated
# hole edge to foreign copper is 0.894 mm at MP4 (3.2x); worst pad-involved hole pair is an
# NPTH-to-via 0.530 mm (1.2x); smallest NPTH drill is 0.991 mm (2.0x). The rules are insurance
# gates, not corrections — the board was already inside JLC's envelope everywhere.
#
# Sources: OSH Park docs (two-layer + After Dark service pages, read 2026-07-27), PCBWay's
# stated 2-layer capability as recorded in this file's previous revision, and
# jlcpcb.com/capabilities/pcb-capabilities (2-layer 1 oz table, read 2026-08-08).
#
# SINGLE-TIER HARD FLOORS — the reasoning below is retained because it still governs.
#
# Why a two-tier scheme does not work here:
#   An earlier revision paired an error floor with a looser marginal-band WARNING. That does not
#   do what it reads like. KiCad resolves ONE effective clearance per object pair — the most
#   restrictive applicable min — and reports under the rule that set it. Because the marginal
#   band's value was LOOSER (larger) than the error floor, the band always won: every tight spot
#   came back as a warning and the error floor never fired, masking genuine sub-floor clearances
#   that would have shipped. Two clearance tiers (error < A, warning < B, A < B) cannot coexist.
#   If you want routing margin, put it in the board's net-class clearance (which the router obeys
#   live) — NOT in a second DRU rule. That is a different mechanism and it composes correctly.
#
# Why the gates sit a hair BELOW the fab minimum:
#   These are "do not ship below this" lines, and geometry built exactly at spec must not
#   coin-flip on floating-point rounding. A 0.1524 mm gap computed as 0.15239999 would fail a
#   0.1524 gate for no physical reason. Each floor is therefore set a fraction under the true
#   limit (0.152 vs 0.1524; 0.1499 vs 0.150) — close enough that nothing physically out of spec
#   passes, loose enough that at-spec geometry does not flicker. This is the same trick the
#   annular rule already used, now applied consistently.

(rule "clearance-hard-floor"
  (severity error)
  (constraint clearance (min 0.152mm)))

(rule "track-hard-floor"
  (severity error)
  (constraint track_width (min 0.152mm)))

# The via fleet is uniform 0.554/0.254 (2026-08-08; was 0.6/0.3) -- the smallest via this
# three-fab envelope permits: OSH Park's 0.254 drill floor plus PCBWay's 0.150 ring on each
# side. The annular is EXACTLY 0.150 by construction, zero margin against PCBWay -- unchanged
# from the old fleet, because the shrink moved pad and drill together and the ring never moved.
# (The panel frame's six plating-bus stitching vias in scripts/panelize.py stay 0.6/0.3 on
# purpose: PCBWay-only scrap carrying plating current, where beefier is simply better.)
(rule "annular-hard-floor"
  (severity error)
  (constraint annular_width (min 0.1499mm)))

(rule "drill-floor"
  (severity error)
  (constraint hole_size (min 0.254mm)))

# OSH Park requires 15 mil of copper pullback from the nominal board edge. The GND pours already
# clear it (0.5005 mm measured), and the board's own min_copper_edge_clearance is 0.5 mm, which is
# stricter still. The known and deliberate exception is the pair of 0.4 mm plating-bus stubs that
# cross the outline at x=25.4 to feed electrolytic hard gold at PCBWay -- they are REQUIRED there
# and PROHIBITED everywhere else, so they are the one object that cannot satisfy all three fabs.
# See PCB/README.md: the OSH Park upload deletes those two stubs, and nothing else. JLCPCB offers
# no selective hard gold either (HASL/ENIG/OSP only), so it takes the SAME stub-less 1-up upload
# as OSH Park -- one deletion procedure covers both ENIG-only fabs.
#
# Those stubs are only complete inside the PCBWay panel (scripts/panelize.py), where they cross a
# break tab onto the frame's bus ring. This DRC gate deliberately runs on the 1-up board and not on
# the panel: the panel adds frame geometry and moves no board object, so gating it twice would only
# add a rule set that has to be kept in sync with this one.
(rule "edge-clearance-floor"
  (severity error)
  (constraint edge_clearance (min 0.381mm)))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JLCPCB-governed floors (2026-08-08). Each is conditioned to the object class JLC constrains,
# so the unconditioned floors above keep governing everything else. Values sit a hair under the
# published limit per the float-safety doctrine at the top of this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# JLC's 1 oz through-hole pads need >= 0.18 mm of annular ring — more than a via (0.05 at JLC,
# 0.1499 gated above by PCBWay). Only the eight M2 mount pads match this condition; they carry
# 0.700 mm.
(rule "jlc-pth-pad-annular-floor"
  (severity error)
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && A.Pad_Type == 'Through-hole'")
  (constraint annular_width (min 0.1799mm)))

# JLC wants 0.28 mm from a plated hole's wall to foreign copper (vias only need 0.2, which the
# board's own hole-clearance setting already enforces). Worst case on this board: 0.894 mm at MP4.
(rule "jlc-pth-hole-to-copper-floor"
  (severity error)
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && A.Pad_Type == 'Through-hole'")
  (constraint hole_clearance (min 0.2799mm)))

# JLC allows via-to-via hole walls at 0.2 mm but wants 0.45 mm the moment a pad's hole is one of
# the pair (PTH or NPTH — both are pads in KiCad, so 'A or B is a Pad' is exactly JLC's class).
# Deliberately NOT applied to via-via pairs: the fleet's measured minimum is 0.458 mm and gating
# it at 0.4499 would leave 9 um of air under every future re-route for no fab reason.
# Worst pad-involved pair on this board: an NPTH-to-via at 0.530 mm.
(rule "jlc-pad-hole-to-hole-floor"
  (severity error)
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' || B.Type == 'Pad'")
  (constraint hole_to_hole (min 0.4499mm)))

# JLC drills no NPTH under 0.50 mm (its 0.15 mm floor gated above is for PLATED holes only).
# The board's seven NPTH are 0.991 and 2.375 mm.
(rule "jlc-npth-drill-floor"
  (severity error)
  (condition "A.Type == 'Pad' && A.Pad_Type == 'NPTH, mechanical'")
  (constraint hole_size (min 0.4999mm)))
